# Retired 28 Jul 2026: the June favicon comparison page. It lived in public/
# and so shipped as a real, indexable route. Moved to content/favicon-options/.
# Needs an explicit rule because the SPA fallback below would otherwise answer
# it with a 200 — a soft 404, which is worse than a redirect for a URL Google
# may already have indexed.
/favicon-options       /  301!
/favicon-options/*     /  301!

# /home-v2 is redirected inside React only (App.jsx). That was enough while the
# rule below answered every unknown path with the SPA, which then handled the
# redirect client-side. Now that unmatched paths get a real 404, a direct hit or
# a crawler on an old shared /home-v2 link would never reach React. Needs to be
# a server-side 301 like the other retired URLs.
/home-v2  /  301!

# Catch-all: a REAL 404, not the SPA shell.
#
# This was `/*  /index.html  200` until 28 Jul 2026, which meant every typo,
# dead link and stale inbound URL returned 200 with the shell — a soft 404.
# Google reads the status code, so the whole site looked like infinite valid
# pages with no content.
#
# Safe because Netlify matches static files BEFORE redirect rules (this rule is
# unforced — no `!`), and since the same day every real route is its own file:
# dist/about.html, dist/work/azarus.html, and so on. Only genuinely unmatched
# paths reach this line. scripts/prerender.mjs guarantees a file exists for
# every sitemap route even when the browser fails to launch, so a bad prerender
# can never turn real pages into 404s.
/*  /404.html  404
